{"name":"Bonaire","hex":"#e6e2d7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bonaire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island, dependent territory, and special municipality of the Netherlands in the Caribbean, off the west coast of Venezuela."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bonaire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonaire","blocks":[{"text":"Bonaire is a Caribbean island in the Leeward Antilles. A special municipality of the Netherlands, its seat is the port of Kralendijk, on the west (leeward) coast of the island. Aruba, Bonaire and Curaçao form the ABC islands, 80 km (50 mi) off the coast of Venezuela. The islands have an arid climate that attracts visitors seeking warm, sunny weather all year round, and they lie outside the Main Development Region for tropical cyclones. Bonaire is a popular snorkeling and scuba diving destination because of its multiple shore diving sites, shipwrecks and easy access to the island's fringing reefs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Flag_of_Bonaire.svg/330px-Flag_of_Bonaire.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonaire","wikidata":"Q25396"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/RINCON_OPEN_AIR_MUSEUM%2C_BONAIRE.jpg/500px-RINCON_OPEN_AIR_MUSEUM%2C_BONAIRE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/RINCON_OPEN_AIR_MUSEUM%2C_BONAIRE.jpg/500px-RINCON_OPEN_AIR_MUSEUM%2C_BONAIRE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional old houses with cactus fences, preserved in the outdoor museum of Rincon, Bonaire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARINCON_OPEN_AIR_MUSEUM%2C_BONAIRE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/OLD_FORT_ORANJE%2C_KRALENDIJK.jpg/500px-OLD_